[size=6][b]⚔ Katars and Knuckledusters[/b][/size]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/MaxYari/Katars-KnucklesOpenMW/main/imgs/banner.png[/img]

Hand-to-hand weapons for OpenMW. Strap a blade or a set of knuckles to your fists and fight with the [b]Hand to Hand[/b] skill - your punches, only with some steel in them.

[b]13 weapons[/b]: 5 katars and 8 sets of knuckledusters, in wood, chitin, iron, steel, silver, orcish, ebony and daedric. [b]3 of them are rare[/b], with a trick of their own each - finding them and working out what they do is up to you. The rest turn up the way ordinary weapons do: in merchants' stock, on NPCs and in chests.

For conjurers there is [b]Bound Fist[/b], a new conjuration spell that binds a daedric hand-to-hand weapon to your fists. Which weapon you get depends on your Conjuration - there are visually different ones to reach as your skill grows. A few spell merchants teach it.

Developed for OpenMW. [b]Requires OpenMW 0.51+[/b].

[url=https://ko-fi.com/maxyari][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/MaxYari/Katars-KnucklesOpenMW/main/imgs/morrowind_kofi_banner_left_half_bright124.gif[/img][/url][url=https://ko-fi.com/maxyari][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/MaxYari/Katars-KnucklesOpenMW/main/imgs/nexus/banner_right.png[/img][/url]
[url=https://ko-fi.com/maxyari][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/MaxYari/Katars-KnucklesOpenMW/main/imgs/nexus/banner_glow.png[/img][/url]

[size=5][b]⚔ What they do[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]The game files katars under Short Blade and knuckledusters under Blunt Weapon, but you fight with both using [b]Hand to Hand[/b]: it decides whether you hit, and it gets most of the experience. Keeping the weapon skill up is worth a small bonus.
[*]Every hit also bruises like a punch, wearing the target's fatigue down until they drop - and once they are down, it hurts. Katars cut harder, knuckledusters bruise harder.
[*]A second copy of the weapon goes in your off hand, and they move and fight with ReAnimation's hand-to-hand animations.
[/list]

[b]Spoiler: what they all look like[/b]
[spoiler]

If you would rather spoil the fun and see every katar and knuckleduster before you find them, here they are:

